{"name":"Orange Caramel","hex":"#de954b","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"orange","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An evergreen tree of the genus Citrus such as Citrus sinensis which yields oranges (the fruit).","Any round citrus fruit with a yellow-red colour when ripe and a sour-sweet taste; the fruit of the orange tree.\n Specifically, a sweet orange or Citrus sinensis."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having the colour of the fruit of an orange tree; yellowred; reddish-yellow."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/orange"},{"term":"caramel","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A smooth, chewy, sticky confection made by heating sugar and other ingredients until the sugars polymerize and become sticky.","A (sometimes hardened) piece of this confection."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a yellow-brown color."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/caramel"}],"entries":[{"title":"Orange Caramel","blocks":[{"text":"Orange Caramel was the first subgroup of South Korean girl group After School. The subgroup was formed in 2010 with the third generation After School members Nana, Raina, and Lizzy."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/50/150331_%EC%98%A4%EB%A0%8C%EC%A7%80%EC%BA%AC%EB%9D%BC%EB%A9%9C_%EA%B3%A0%EB%A0%A4%EB%8C%80_%EB%AF%BC%EC%A3%BC%EA%B4%91%EC%9E%A5_%EA%B0%84%EC%8B%9D%EC%9D%B4%EB%B2%A4%ED%8A%B8.jpg/330px-150331_%EC%98%A4%EB%A0%8C%EC%A7%80%EC%BA%AC%EB%9D%BC%EB%A9%9C_%EA%B3%A0%EB%A0%A4%EB%8C%80_%EB%AF%BC%EC%A3%BC%EA%B4%91%EC%9E%A5_%EA%B0%84%EC%8B%9D%EC%9D%B4%EB%B2%A4%ED%8A%B8.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Orange_Caramel","wikidata":"Q181144"},{"title":"Orange Caramel (album)","blocks":[{"text":"Orange Caramel is the debut Japanese studio album by South Korean girl group After School sub-unit Orange Caramel. It was released on March 13, 2013, by Avex Trax. The album was preceded by the singles \"Yasashii Akuma\" and \"Lipstick/Lamu no Love Song\"."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/0/0b/OCJapanC.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Orange_Caramel_(album)","wikidata":"Q7099526"},{"title":"Caramel","blocks":[{"text":"Caramel is a range of food ingredients made by heating sugars to high temperatures. It is used as a flavoring in puddings and desserts, as a filling in bonbons or candy bars, as a topping for ice cream and custard, and as a colorant commonly used in drinks."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/89/Caramel-2.jpg/330px-Caramel-2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Caramel","wikidata":"Q183440"},{"title":"Orange (colour)","blocks":[{"text":"Orange is the colour between yellow and red on the spectrum of visible light. The human eyes perceive orange when observing light with a dominant wavelength between roughly 585 and 620 nanometres. In traditional colour theory, it is a secondary colour of pigments, produced by mixing yellow and red. In the RGB colour model, it is a tertiary colour. It is named after the fruit of the same name."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d8/Delicatearch.png/330px-Delicatearch.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Orange_(colour)","wikidata":"Q39338"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/87/101229_sbs%EA%B0%80%EC%9A%94%EB%8C%80%EC%A0%84-%EC%98%A4%EB%A0%8C%EC%A7%80%EC%B9%B4%EB%9D%BC%EB%A9%9C_%282%29.jpg/500px-101229_sbs%EA%B0%80%EC%9A%94%EB%8C%80%EC%A0%84-%EC%98%A4%EB%A0%8C%EC%A7%80%EC%B9%B4%EB%9D%BC%EB%A9%9C_%282%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/87/101229_